Does anyone else have a lettering scheme for their inventory items? I 
always put certain items in certain letter slots, because my fingers 
have gotten used to using those key combinations. I've assumed that 
everyone else does the same thing, but now I'm actually wondering if 
this is the case.

For me, the big ones are my left hand (on a Dvorak keyboard, the left 
home row is aoeui):
a - useful applied item, varies: camera, polearm, etc
o - pickaxe
e - magic whistle
E - lockpick/key/credit card
u - unihorn
i - stethoscope
j - BoH
q and k - other bags, sometimes.
Q - quivered item, usually daggers
f - blindfold/towel
F - /oCancel sack, always labeled "/oCANCEL IN HERE! - F"
w - main weapon, for easy (w)ielding.

All but f and w are on the left hand on Dvorak, so I can play a lot 
without moving my righthand from the numpad.

Any other items you think are used enough to merit a permanent key?

